WEBVTT

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:15.390
M4A1's team began a mission to save AR15.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:18.470
When the Sangvis dolls
suddenly lost control,

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:21.270
her team was able to
succeed in rescuing AR15.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.310
You really came, M4A1?

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:32.070
As you know, AR15 is in our hands.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:36.820
A human commander has the right
to give her orders right now.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.240
She can't make that decision on her own.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:46.710
The Sangvis dolls have
started shooting each other.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:50.340
We don't know why, but this is our chance.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:53.470
Destroy the Sangvis, Commander Gentiane.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.880
I broke your legs.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:58.550
Your speed is a threat,
even if the rest of you isn't.

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:02.680
How do you have Sangvis command authority?

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:06.810
I may be special, huh, Hunter?

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.450
"S09 Mountaintop City Region"

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:27.040
Sangvis Patrol at ten o'clock,
300 meters away.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.880
Maintain a distance of over
30 meters from the enemy.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.920
Encircle and wipe them out.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.170
Go.

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:36.880
Fire!

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:52.650
This is so easy!

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:56.860
Our combat efficiency is
much higher than before!

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:59.740
It's thanks to M4's leadership!

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:00.870
No...

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:03.830
Check your ammo, and let's go.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:41.220
Griffin dispatched an investigation
team into S09 a few days ago.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:44.090
"18 Hours Before Mission Start"

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:44.090
Griffin dispatched an investigation
team into S09 a few days ago.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:49.310
Their route takes them
through Sangvis territory.

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:53.100
In other words, it's likely
they'll be attacked.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:56.940
The brass has ordered
us to provide support.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:59.360
The other commanders
don't know this, I think,

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:04.240
but we've made strikes
on S09 several times.

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:07.580
The number of Sangvis there has
not decreased at all, however.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.830
That place is bad news.

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:12.120
Judging from our past combat data,

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.710
the Sangvis are likely
to ambush us here...

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:16.130
...here...

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:17.170
...here...

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:19.130
...and here.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:22.510
Of course, don't forget
to watch the other areas.

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:26.550
That's where we found M4!

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:27.720
Yup!

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.760
It's outside the primary mission area,

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.390
but it's an area you've got
a lot of memories of, right?

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:36.100
I'd rather not ever go there again.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.360
S-Sorry...

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:42.320
The only thing HQ sent us
was the predicted route.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:44.610
It's probably a special team.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:49.580
Thus, our job will be to draw
the enemy away from them.

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:50.740
That's all.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:52.830
If you have questions, ask them now.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:57.750
Otherwise, get some sleep tonight.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:00.170
Gather up at 0445 tomorrow.

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:02.800
We leave at 0500.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:04.010
Dismissed!

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.270
Did you forget what the commander
told you this afternoon?

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:19.060
Get some sleep.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:22.940
I'm not starting a mission
with a tired leader.

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:25.820
That goes for you too, AR15.

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:29.700
Unlike a certain someone who keeps
fiddling with a Sangvis eyeball all day,

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:32.370
I get my rest.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:37.620
I still get nervous before missions.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:41.500
It's a slightly different
nervousness this time, though.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:46.220
And the place the commander
was talking about this afternoon.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:49.300
We had a similar discussion before, right?

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:52.470
Yeah? I don't remember.

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:57.940
We're warriors, and weapons.

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:00.810
We've dedicated everything
we have to our victory.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:03.780
That's all we need to focus on.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:07.650
M4, we'll find her.

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:08.990
Together.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.530
Yeah.

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:14.080
I'll be counting on you tomorrow.

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:16.660
Of course.

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:22.540
Was I worried over nothing?

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:27.170
But...

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:31.220
Why did the Sangvis suddenly
go out of control?

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:35.600
And how did AR15 escape from her bonds?

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:39.230
Well, even a new commander
like me is wondering.

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:42.110
I'm sure the top brass have a good idea.

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:49.650
"4 Hours After Mission Start"

00:06:50.030 --> 00:06:51.360
This doesn't make sense.

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:52.700
What's wrong?

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:55.160
It's going well, right?.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:57.160
Yes, the enemy's not that strong.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:00.620
But they just keep coming.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:04.500
It's been four hours since
the mission started.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:07.960
There are a lot of enemies
in this region, sure.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:11.180
But it's bizarre that there'd be
no gaps in the fighting at all.

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:15.930
Kalina, prepare a level three
satellite scan at V6J8A.

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:16.930
Huh?

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:19.770
You're using a recon satellite?

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:20.940
All right.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:25.070
It'll take 22 minutes to get the
nearest recon satellite ready.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:27.530
All 794 units, halt.

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:30.400
Find a good place to hide and stand by.

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:35.990
Unit 3, come here.

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:37.200
Roger!

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:45.960
West side clear.

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:47.670
East side clear.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:01.270
Everyone, I found something.

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:05.270
Bullet holes from an elite Sangvis's
large-caliber plasma cannon.

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:20.580
What is this?

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:29.170
I knew it.

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:37.180
That's G43.

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:39.760
Which means this is...

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:45.650
The place where we were attacked
by Agents two months ago.

00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:48.400
Did you know?

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:49.270
Yes.

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:53.900
But that mission was highly classified.

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:56.110
I couldn't tell the commander.

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:02.910
Should we bring back this G43 body?

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:07.670
Or leave a marker for one of the
base's drones to recover it later?

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:11.090
No, let's let her rest here.

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:12.210
But...

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:13.590
Don't worry.

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:17.840
Commander Gentiane has already
ordered a new doll of the same type.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:20.010
I just saved her affiliation code,

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:24.350
so now we can install a back up
of her mind inside the new body.

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:26.390
Oh, right.

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:28.520
There are backups, aren't there?

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:38.660
Thank you for all your hard work.

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:40.830
Now rest.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:45.250
We'll watch things outside!

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:56.760
Being sentimental won't change a thing.

00:09:56.760 --> 00:10:00.890
She fought with us.

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:05.560
I won't leave anyone else behind.

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:16.240
"11 Hours Before Mission Start"

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:22.740
We've arrived at the point.

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:25.250
Two minutes ahead of schedule.

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:29.670
A human commander makes
things so much better.

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:33.000
416, do what you're told, okay?

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.880
I don't need your advice.

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:37.720
I'll follow orders. That's all.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:40.760
So, this is the spot, right?

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:42.970
Of course it is.

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:49.520
This is where AR Team got
their asses kicked by two Agents.

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:53.520
Is there time for rejoicing in
old memories here, you think?

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:56.030
Want me to scrap you?

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:02.490
Data restoration complete.

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:04.580
Agents' coordinates confirmed.

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:07.540
Okay. Mission complete.

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:10.920
So, 416, what were you doing?

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:14.710
Oh, you were looking for
clues to their whereabouts.

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:16.840
This is the best chance I'll get.

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:19.220
I can't miss it.

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:22.470
Okay. I won't get in your way.

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:26.560
I'll look at the data 9 found first.

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:31.270
Oh, right.

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:33.770
Don't have too much fun.

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:38.360
I'm sure you know how dangerous
they can be when they're serious.

00:11:42.450 --> 00:11:44.820
That's all the information I have.

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:49.830
All data from myself, Scarecrow,
and Executioner has been uploaded.

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:55.540
So M4A1 still has the Safehouse 3 data.

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:57.800
They don't seem to have done much with it.

00:11:57.800 --> 00:12:01.340
Griffin must not know what it's worth.

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:05.550
The information about Plan Parapluie,
or the information about the "remains."

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:08.100
Either way, my mission ends.

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:10.230
I'm going back to my hunting.

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:12.730
Such a barbarian!

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:17.400
Why are all my soldiers like this?

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:21.490
I refuse to sit and wait for death
in my best outfit, like you.

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:25.660
And that's why you'll never
be anything more than a pawn.

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:30.080
Do you regret coming to work for me?

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:32.290
I never had a choice.

00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:36.250
If I can die and be rid of you,
that'll be enough for me.

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:37.710
Don't worry.

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:41.590
I've saved all your data.

00:12:41.590 --> 00:12:47.470
My job here is to prepare
for your last great goodbye.

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:49.470
What is this?

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:53.850
A record of a report from
Sangvis Ringleaders,

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:59.940
which we fought a Sangvis enhanced
defense team for seven hours to acquire.

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:02.110
Our commander told us not to worry

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:05.240
since there weren't any powerful
enemies there, though.

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:07.870
I-I understand.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:11.290
The Sangvis sure talk, huh?

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:14.330
They were probably
set up like that, right?

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:18.170
All Sangvis dolls have
flawed personalities, right?

00:13:18.170 --> 00:13:20.550
Like our commander.

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:24.470
Has your personality changed?

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:28.390
This is a difficult bit of
information we've gathered.

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:31.770
What do we do with it? Destroy it?

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:35.520
No, this is a critical
mission for Griffin.

00:13:35.520 --> 00:13:37.810
We can't get rid of it.

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:42.730
I remembered just now...

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:49.570
About my angel, who knows all about S09
and will do anything if there's a reward.

00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:56.870
You know, Commander Shi Jun
asked me on a date.

00:13:56.870 --> 00:13:58.460
Huh?

00:13:58.460 --> 00:13:59.920
Surprising, huh?

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:03.710
So, what did you say?

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:05.300
Well...

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:09.340
Recon satellite is in position.

00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:10.800
The data's here.

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:12.260
Put it on the monitor.

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:13.470
Roger!

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:19.350
Look... We defeated a bunch,
but there are more than ever, right?

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:22.270
What are the Sangvis, anyway?

00:14:22.270 --> 00:14:24.860
A virus or something?

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:27.200
Helian, what is it?

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:30.660
I'll make this short, Commander.

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:34.200
We've gotten information in
from that team we deployed.

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:38.120
Unlike during our recon,
things aren't looking good.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:39.170
Yes.

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:41.920
I found the same thing via satellite scan.

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:46.380
The reason is that a new Sangvis
Ringleader has appeared.

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:48.930
Her name is Intruder.

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:50.800
Intruder...

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:51.800
Yes.

00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:54.430
She's a new type,

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:58.690
and we have no information on her
in our existing product catalogs.

00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:00.900
What little we know indicates that

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:05.360
unlike previous Sangvis Ringleaders,
this one specializes in commanding troops.

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:07.240
So it seems.

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:09.990
But your mission remains the same.

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:14.330
Continue to draw the Sangvis's attention
to keep them from sending in troops.

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:16.330
Don't let them onto the battlefield.

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:17.540
Roger.

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:24.460
But we don't have nearly the ammo
we'd need to fight this many Sangvis.

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:28.260
Shall we use helicopters and
drones to set up a supply point?

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:29.510
Go for it.

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:32.890
What was supposed to be a picnic
has turned into a game of tag.

00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:36.720
Let's start with the bases
that are under Sangvis control.

00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:38.600
Show me the comm traffic heatmap.

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:39.810
Okay.

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:42.810
I see.

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:45.520
If nothing else,
they're not trying to hide.

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:49.400
N94 command post to all units.

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:51.360
We're changing the plan.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:54.030
Units 1 and 2 join up.

00:15:54.030 --> 00:15:57.120
Unit 3, head to coordinates FB1CX.

00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:58.700
I'll give you the details later.

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:00.040
Head there now.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:01.790
Roger.

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:03.080
Come in.

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:05.840
AR Team, can you hear me?

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:07.300
M16?

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:08.630
Big Sis M16?

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:10.880
M16 is okay?

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:12.340
What happened?

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:17.140
It appears word has come in from
the missing member of the AR Team.

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:20.020
Is that you, M4?

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:21.850
Did you all meet up?

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:23.020
Everyone's here!

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:24.940
You're the last one!

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:26.440
Glad to hear it.

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:27.400
Don't worry.

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:29.190
I'm fine.

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:31.110
I found a supply point, too.

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:33.660
But I've still got something to do.

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:34.990
You do?

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:37.410
When are you coming back?

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:40.500
I still don't know.

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:42.250
I'm hanging up.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:44.620
Hello? Hello? Big Sis?

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:46.500
Big Sis M16?

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:49.050
She's always like this.

00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:50.960
Calm down.

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:53.470
At least we know she's safe.

00:16:53.470 --> 00:16:55.640
She may be nearby.

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:58.760
Let's go looking as soon as
we're done with this mission.

00:17:00.140 --> 00:17:03.100
Thank you, Commander Gentiane.

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:09.020
After all that big talk I did,

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:12.440
I wish I had somebody to help me.

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:16.700
Of course, I don't think
you're here to help!

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:21.490
Oh dear...

00:17:21.490 --> 00:17:24.120
Would you have preferred Sangvis?

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:27.790
No, I saw this coming.

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:32.420
But if you're part of Griffin and
still killing dolls that aren't Sangvis,

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:35.260
I'd at least like to know why,

00:17:35.260 --> 00:17:36.840
416!

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:39.220
Squad 404 has special privileges.

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:42.220
We're allowed to launch preemptive
attacks on anybody who gets in our way,

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:44.100
enemy or ally.

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:48.100
How convenient. I'm jealous.

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:50.400
Shut up, M16!

00:17:51.860 --> 00:17:55.240
You understand what the price of that is!

00:17:58.870 --> 00:18:02.200
What, am I in the way that much?

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:07.040
To be honest, I was never happy
about being given this privilege.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:08.960
Except today!

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:11.000
I'll be honest, too.

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:16.300
When I was at the National Safety
Agency, I quite liked you.

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:18.470
Shut up, M16!

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:23.180
There!

00:18:27.020 --> 00:18:28.230
She's not there?

00:18:33.110 --> 00:18:36.190
You lose, M16.

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:38.660
Right, right.

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:42.580
You win.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:58.630
I told you before.

00:18:58.630 --> 00:19:01.180
It's good to be able to hide.

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:04.220
But don't rely on that skill too much.

00:19:20.030 --> 00:19:21.280
Why?

00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:25.040
I'm the superior doll!

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:28.370
Experience, responses, training...

00:19:28.370 --> 00:19:30.580
You don't have enough of any of those.

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:32.250
You're always like that.

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:35.750
What am I to you?

00:19:35.750 --> 00:19:37.920
Do you want to know that badly?

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:41.380
I'll tell you then, 416.

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:44.430
You're nothing to me.

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:45.970
Do you understand?

00:19:45.970 --> 00:19:50.100
You are of no value to me.
I have no interest in you.

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:51.770
You're nothing at all.

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:55.690
That's why I don't like you, M16!

00:19:55.690 --> 00:20:00.070
No matter what happens, you always
act like you know everything.

00:20:00.070 --> 00:20:03.280
You never show the slightest weakness!

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:12.170
Every doll has emotions, on some level.

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:15.000
That's what makes us difficult.

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:19.170
Right now, somebody is
waiting for my return.

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:21.220
I'm in a hurry.

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:24.300
So get lost, 416.

00:20:26.100 --> 00:20:30.930
You don't want a real fight
with me either, do you?

00:20:30.930 --> 00:20:32.270
I see.

00:20:32.270 --> 00:20:34.940
So, that's your weakness.

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:38.440
Shut up.

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:42.150
And don't forget what happened here.

00:20:42.150 --> 00:20:43.700
Otherwise...

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:47.870
...I'll make it so the only answer
your AI can generate is "suicide."

00:20:55.500 --> 00:21:00.920
416's gone. You can come out, UMP45.

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:03.300
You saw me, huh?

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:08.260
I was sure I'd concealed myself.

00:21:08.260 --> 00:21:10.850
I'm on my way out.

00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:14.520
Don't tell me you came to
clean up the mess 416 caused.

00:21:14.520 --> 00:21:17.690
On your way out? I don't know about that.

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:21.690
You still have your secret
weapon on your back.

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:25.410
This isn't for you.

00:21:25.410 --> 00:21:27.410
Glad to hear it.

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:32.200
I just came to get 416 on
my way home from a job.

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:36.790
She worked hard,
so I gave her some time off.

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:41.420
And she used that time to
come interfere with me?

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:47.470
You're the only ones
who act like this, UMP45.

00:21:47.470 --> 00:21:49.050
Don't worry.

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:52.810
416 won't kill you.

00:21:52.810 --> 00:21:57.230
She was just kind of upset,
and came to complain.

00:21:57.230 --> 00:21:58.650
I know.

00:21:58.650 --> 00:22:01.440
That's why I let her live.

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:03.070
I know.

00:22:03.070 --> 00:22:05.820
And that's why I'll let you live.

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:13.080
Good to hear.

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:14.870
We have a deal, then.

00:22:14.870 --> 00:22:19.920
But if you go back now,
you'll just get killed, M16.

00:22:21.210 --> 00:22:24.260
Don't underestimate 16LAB's technology.

00:22:24.260 --> 00:22:26.840
I won't die so easily.

00:22:26.840 --> 00:22:30.970
So? Did you learn anything
on your mission?

00:22:30.970 --> 00:22:34.140
The rain fell. On the plains.

00:22:34.140 --> 00:22:36.350
Rain? Plains?

00:22:36.350 --> 00:22:37.600
What does that mean?

00:22:37.600 --> 00:22:41.650
Your creator may know.

00:22:47.320 --> 00:22:49.410
I'll be going.

00:22:49.410 --> 00:22:52.410
Oh, if you see your friends...

00:22:52.410 --> 00:22:56.080
I'll tell them you're already dead.

00:22:56.080 --> 00:22:58.370
Right.

00:22:58.370 --> 00:23:01.040
Bye. See you next time.

00:23:07.630 --> 00:23:11.220
I hope there is no next time.

00:24:43.100 --> 00:24:46.520
Episode 7: "The Message 02."
